WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.068
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.435
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.304
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:09.142
You're watching at home,
thank you.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.277
Hey, just so you guys know,
while you were cheering,

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.580
three more billionaires
launched themselves into space.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.782
So isn't that...

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.484
Yeah, it was an exciting day,

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.285
'cause just after 9:00
this morning,

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.954
Jeff Bezos flew to space aboard

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:24.257
Blue Origin's
New Shepherd rocket.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.059
If you didn't see the launch,
here it is.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.965
-Go, Jeff. Go, Mark.
Go, Wally. Go, Oliver.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:34.634
You are going to space.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.569
-Yeah.

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:41.274
First Branson, now Bezos.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.343
Tomorrow, Warren Buffett is
gonna try to get up there with

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.945
balloons like the old guy
from "Up."

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.484
That's right --
Bezos was launched into space,

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.053
which is the natural career
progression for anyone who

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:57.356
starts an online bookstore.

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.058
Before his trip
to space, Bezos said,

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.426
"I'm just really
excited to figure out

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:02.962
how it's going to change me."

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.931
Well, here he is
before the flight.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.067
And this is real.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.669
Here he is after he landed.

00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:13.906
-Oh!

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.040
-That's not real.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.809
-I guess space turns you
into Kenny Chesney.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:20.046
I don't know what...

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.114
That's right -- Bezos actually
wore a cowboy hat

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:23.149
for today's flight.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.684
Can we see it again?

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.253
You know you're rich when
you put that on

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.622
and everyone who works for you
goes, "Oh, it looks great.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.957
Yeah.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.860
You're a man of the people,
just going to space.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:36.696
Let me see it again one more...

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:43.002
He looks like a mash-up between
Buzz Lightyear and Woody.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:48.341
[ Applause ]
Two for one.

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.545
Yeah, he got the space suit
and the cowboy hat together

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.949
by searching for
the mid-life crisis bundle.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.618
"Is a soul patch too much?"

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.919
But Bezos wasn't alone.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:02.087
He was joined by three
other people in the capsule.

00:02:02.087 --> 00:02:03.089
Here's everyone together.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.724
Yep, the first space crew to get

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:08.194
their portrait done at Walmart.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.331
They look like they're about
to do the 2:45 show

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:15.435
at the main pool at SeaWorld.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:19.439
-[ Barks ]
-Can I see it again?

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.974
Let me see -- There you go.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:25.745
It looks like a portrait of
Mr. Clean's family.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:29.582
The crew included 82-year-old
pilot Wally Funk,

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.318
who became the oldest
astronaut in history.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.454
And at one point,
you could sort of tell.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:36.523
Listen to this. This is real.

00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:01.915
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:09.455
Then she almost pushed
the launch button.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.891
They're like, "No, Wally, no!
Don't..."

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.526
Feel like every Zoom
with grandma.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:17.764
It's like, "Just push 'unmute.'
Push -- No, that's your camera.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.499
Don't -- Just call grandma."

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:21.801
Well, a lot of people
were talking about

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.936
the shape of the rocket.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:25.305
Can we see a photo of it?

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:30.943
It kind of looks like --
Well, I mean,

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.277
why would you design it
like that?

00:03:32.277 --> 00:03:35.514 line:0%
I just -- Anyway, let's just put
30 seconds on the clock

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.383 line:0%
and see how many jokes
we can do here.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.751 line:0%
You want to get in on
this, Tariq?

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.520 line:0%
-Oh, you know it.
-Alright, here we go.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.623 line:0%
It's the only rocket that
shrinks in the cold.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:46.625 line:0%
-They designed it at
the Johnson Space Center.

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:49.329 line:0%
-It looks like R2-D2
took some Viagra.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.730 line:0%
-They don't keep it in a hangar.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.001 line:0%
They keep it in the top drawer
of a bedside table.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:58.671 line:0%
-Right after the launch,
the rocket goes into sleep mode.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:01.340 line:0%
-I'm surprised news channels
didn't have to blur that.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.576 line:0%
-Next stop, the "O"-zone.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:07.580 line:0%
-It's not that hard
to get to space.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.016 line:0%
-Well, it took a long time
to erect it.

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:14.053 line:0%
-Guys, I got one.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:18.257 line:0%
-It looks like someone undid
their asteroid belt.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.525 line:0%
-I got one. I got one.
-What?

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.628 line:0%
-It looks like male genitalia.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:24.330 line:0%
[ Ding ]
-Oh.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.366 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.502
Wow.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:33.839
-Alright, changing gears.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.073
Hey, this is fun.

00:04:35.073 --> 00:04:37.710
I saw that Disney just unveiled
the first look at

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.979
Joe Biden's robot at
the Hall of Presidents.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.080
-Ooh!
-Check this out.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.750
-Oh.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.219
-They can't seem to
master these, yeah?

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.220
He looks like
he opened the fridge

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.490
and can't decide what to eat.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.863
"Activia.
Prunes. I don't know."

00:04:57.863 --> 00:04:59.866
It's not great, but can we
take a look at Trump's?

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:06.372
Well, alright,
maybe Biden's isn't so bad.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.774
Finally, on last night's episode
of "The Bachelorette,"

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:12.411
there was a pretty interesting
scene between Katie and Mike P.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:14.513
We love "The Bachelorette"
here on the show.

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:16.416
But those scenes
can get pretty emotional.

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:17.549
So I thought that we could help.

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.752
Here's a clip from
the episode re-voiced

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:22.588
with the least-emotional person
we know -- Siri.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.258
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.492
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.194
-[ Whispering ]
"Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.495
♪♪

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:32.230
-"She is a nurturer,
and, man, do I love nurturers.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.532
She reminds me of my mom.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:34.533
Your legs are soft."

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.102
"Oh, well, thank you. Ha ha."

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:39.404
My mom brings a
nurturing touch to everything

00:05:39.404 --> 00:05:42.075
and every situation
that she comes in contact with.

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:43.508
Katie does the same thing."

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:45.078
You remind me of my mom."

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.746
"Really?"

